Subject: [PATCH 11010/11171] Correct the engine count, and record why the
 scoring half found nothing

Two corrections and one finding.

The run emitted four engines, not the two the note claimed: 02:05, 06:24, 07:12
and 07:49Z. That makes the cadence roughly one per 1.7 hours rather than the one
per 4.7 I reported at the four-hour mark, so the first long gap was the outlier
and not the rate. The structural reading in the note rests on engines 1 and 2;
3 and 4 are unexamined.

exp6968, the held-out scoring half, ran at 07:52Z -- three minutes after this
run finished, so there was no concurrency collision -- and blocked in 0.097s
with zero engine_resolution rows. It reads induction_attempts from the run
diagnostics to get a target engine hash, then globs attempts by that hash. The
eval artifact has no induction_attempts field, so there was no hash, so nothing
to glob. Four complete engines sit on disk and the tool built to score them
cannot find them.

That is the same gap as generator_channels, which I wired yesterday: the
generation side records what the generator returned but not which engines it
emitted, when, or against which transition source. The audit needs that triple.

Records a second defect in the reporting rather than the logic: the artifact
blames immutable_transition_source, which is the early-return sentinel appended
with a hardcoded False when an earlier gate fails, before the transition source
is examined at all. A reader would investigate the wrong thing. Same class as
the conductor's artifact_not_updated_past_bootstrap naming the wrong path.

Deliberately not wiring induction_attempts now: it would be the third instance of
this pattern in three days and deserves designing once rather than one field at a
time as each consumer discovers it is missing.

